# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Private working records. These are NOT part of the archive: the analysis
# hand-off is a planning document (venue strategy, unpublished paper plans),
# and the packaging notes are internal QA. Both live outside the repo; these
# patterns are belt-and-braces in case a copy is ever placed here.
TELECONNECTION_ANALYSIS_HANDOFF.md
ZENODO_PACKAGING_NOTES.md

# Bulk pipeline inputs and working intermediates: either input the Caravan
# authors distribute themselves, or output regenerable from this code. The
# derived products behind the paper are the exception and ARE tracked, in
# derived_data/ (see its README).
/caravan_raw/
/caravan_states/
/caravan_derived/
/calibrated_params_caravan/
*.parquet
*.log
!derived_data/*.parquet

# Rendered figures are not tracked. The figures/fig*.py scripts write them,
# and the published copies live with the paper in the manuscript repository.
# Figure 3 is the one that needs more than derived_data/: its panel (a) reads
# the daily state series, which generate_states.py regenerates.
figures/*.png
figures/*.pdf
figures/scratch/
